SHOPGRAPH — CATEGORY MANAGER COMPLETION PIPELINE UPDATE
======================================================

TASK
----

Modify the attached/current ShopGraph codebase to add a new Category Manager
completion workflow.

The goal is to create a second LLM-assisted classification stage that occurs
AFTER ShopGraph has created/refreshed the Category Manager worksheet.

The existing ShopGraph taxonomy is:

    Common Name
        ↓
    Sub-Category
        ↓
    Category

Purchase History stores:

    Common Name
    Sub-Category

The Category Manager worksheet maps:

    Category
        ↓
    Sub-Category
        ↓
    Common Names / Products

The new workflow is specifically responsible for completing missing broad
Category assignments in Category Manager.

Do NOT redesign the existing taxonomy architecture.

Do NOT add broad Category to Purchase History.

Do NOT replace the existing Category Manager.

Extend the existing architecture conservatively.


============================================================
CURRENT RELEVANT WORKFLOW
============================================================

ShopGraph currently contains:

    Data Base Builder
        → Category Manager
            → Create / Refresh Category Manager

When Category Manager is refreshed, products and Sub-Categories are rebuilt
from Purchase History while existing valid:

    Sub-Category → Category

mappings are preserved.

New or unmapped Sub-Categories can therefore appear in Category Manager with:

    Category = NA

The user currently reaches this through:

    ShopGraph
        → Utilities
            → Data Base Builder
                → Category Manager
                    → Create / Refresh Category Manager


